#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
dtSat — Vintage NASA/NORAD & Amateur Radio Satellite Pass & Doppler Tracker for CDE

Features:
  - Authentic 1980s/1990s Cheyenne Mountain / NASA Mission Control workstation console
    styled for CDE (OSF/Motif 3D bevels, xrdb palette sync, glowing VFD readouts)
  - Pure-Python SGP4/J2 Secular & Short-Period Perturbation Orbital Propagator:
      * Standard 3-line NORAD TLE parser (Modulo-10 checksums, B* & ndot drag)
      * Iterative Newton-Raphson Kepler solver, J2 nodal regression & apsidal precession
      * GMST Earth rotation, ECI -> ECEF -> WGS84 Geodetic Lat/Lon/Alt/Velocity
      * Topocentric Azimuth, Elevation, Slant Range & Range-Rate from W1AW [FN31pr]
  - 15 Built-in Iconic Spacecraft TLEs (100% offline ready) + Live CelesTrak Updater
    (amateur, weather, stations cached to ~/.cache/dtsat/tles.txt)
  - Vintage NORAD World Map (Gtk.DrawingArea):
      * Embedded crisp vector continents/lakes, US/international borders, graticule & Maidenhead grid
      * Switchable NORAD CYAN/BLUE, P31 PHOSPHOR GREEN, and AMBER TACTICAL themes
      * Astronomical Solar Day/Night Terminator, W1AW [FN31pr] beacon, 3-orbit ground track,
        live spherical radio-visibility footprint, and active Line-of-Sight vector
  - Circular Az/El Polar Sky-Dome Radar:
      * Horizon/30°/60° rings, N/E/S/W compass, all visible satellites, and full
        AOS -> MAX EL -> LOS pass trajectory arc with 1-minute tick marks
  - Glowing VFD Telemetry Banner + Live Full-Duplex Amateur & Weather Doppler Computer
  - Interactive Fanfold Greenbar 24-Hour Pass Predictor Table (click any pass to preview)
"""

